QR block/capacity, BCH, placement and Reed-Solomon parameters are normative
Model 2 data. The 6,953-scalar Kanji map follows the owner's canonical WHATWG
Shift_JIS first mapping. See kanji.go for generator and digest provenance.
The independent URL implementation has a documented bounded Unicode 15.0.0
hostname profile; see docs/gs1.md. Generated Unicode data retains the Unicode
License v3 in LICENSE-UNICODE. Original Go code is MIT licensed. Combined
redistribution includes MIT AND Unicode-3.0 obligations.

Go standard-library image/png provides PNG compression/serialization;
encoding/base64 provides data URL encoding. PNG pixel output is deterministic,
while compressed bytes are not promised stable between Go versions.
Independent Nayuki, jsQR, ZXing-C++ and ZXing Java are development-only
verification oracles under their own distribution licenses. No oracle source
is linked to the Go library or production CLI.
